        "problem": "Consider a $8\\times 7$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim(Null(}A))=2,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
        "worked_solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =7 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =7 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =7-2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
